<%# M14 ④ the investor email (bank-detail-change-controls H7, E27, E29; task U.1): what changed (account numbers as
    their last 4 digits only), who changed it and when, why this person got it and what to do if they did not ask
    for it. Dates through bare l(...) → "Nov 09, 2026" (EmailDateLocalization). No magic link: "View KYC" opens the
    KYC page after sign-in. A firm's own wording (custom notification) replaces the body; the safety lines stay. %>
<% change = @bank_detail_change %>
<% firm = @investor_kyc.entity.name %>
<% if @custom_notification %>

    <%= render "/custom_notifications/mail" %>

<% else %>

    <p>Dear <%= @user&.full_name.presence || "Investor" %>,</p>

    <p>The bank details on the KYC of <strong><%= @investor_kyc.full_name %></strong> with <%= firm %> were changed<% if change %>
       on <%= l(change.created_at.to_date) %> by <%= change.maker_name %><% end %>.</p>

    <% if change %>
      <ul>
        <% change.email_change_lines.each do |line| %>
          <li><%= line.upcase_first %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
      <p><small>For your security only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown.</small></p>
    <% end %>

<% end %>

<p><strong>If you asked for this, no action is needed.</strong> Distributions are paid to the new account once an
   approver at <%= firm %> has verified it.</p>

<p><strong>If you did not ask for this change, contact <%= firm %> straight away</strong> on a phone number you
   already have for them (not one given in an email), so they can stop any payment to the new account. Do not reply
   to this email with your bank details.</p>

<p><small>You are receiving this because you are a contact for the KYC of <%= @investor_kyc.full_name %> with
   <%= firm %>. CapHive emails every change of a KYC's account number or bank code to the investor's contacts, so a
   change nobody asked for cannot go unnoticed.</small></p>

<p class="btn btn-outline-primary"><%= link_to "View KYC", investor_kyc_url(@investor_kyc, subdomain: @investor_kyc.entity.sub_domain) %></p>
